    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d845">

                <pb facs="1535" n="1501" sameAs="frus:frus1948v02/pg1501"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Council/4–3048: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        United States Deputy for Austria at the Council of Foreign Ministers</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reber</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">at London</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-04-30T17:00:00-04:00">April 30, 1948—5
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1545. For Reber. As suggested Ausdel 6<anchor n="1" xml:id="d845-f1"/> concur
                    re importance maintaining first para Art 2 and agree also re finding some way
                    eliminating para 2 same Art (urtel 1803<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d845-f2"/>). Brit suggestion respecting separate Three Power
                    protocol of guarantee, presumably of a secret nature, is not acceptable to us.
                    We would be willing to consider participating at appropriate time in a
                    declaration similar to President’s statement on occasion Allied troop withdrawal
                    from Italy. In our view, Austrian security is related to western union security
                    and arrangements for latter should envisage eventual Austrian inclusion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
